I've recently wasted 16 healers trying the protection racket.  Two did
make it to mine town and got protection, but I was careless with them
subsequently and they got killed, one by choking on a rothe corpse,
which I shall take as a lesson.  The whole thing has been a learning
experience (I've never got far in this game) and has taught me more
about staying alive in a few days than years of playing had
previously.  I recommend it to new players even if only for the
lessons it teaches.

Anyway, my 17th healer has made it, with a very strong pet, and has
had the added advantage of having found a wand of wishing.  There was
only one charge in it, but I used that for charging scrolls, and then
got GDSM and, with strength only 7, a BoH.  There should be one charge
left, I think.  It's currently tucked away in my bag.  With donations
for protection I'm now AC-10, with only two items of armour - starting
gloves and +2 GDSM - I'm not used to monsters missing me so much.
There's loads of stuff scattered about on the upper mine levels, which
I'll go back for later.

I can get an extra wish out of the wand if I persevere with it, I
believe.  Is this worth it, or will I try for ages with little chance
of success?

I don't see a need to use the last normal wish for the moment.  I
don't want to wish for any artifacts.  The wishing spoiler says I can
wish for up to 20 missile weapons, but I'm thinking daggers don't
count as missile weapons, which is a shame.  A stack of 20 silver
daggers would be useful, I reckon.  Anyway, any suggestions for that
last guaranteed wish?  Or shall I save it?  The mines entrance was on
Dlvl2, so I've not explored very far yet.

Anyway, I still have one blessed scroll of charging, a bag of tricks
(lucky, eh), and a co-aligned altar in mine town.  This gives me a
sanctuary which, as I'm still level 1 (just 2 experience points), will
be useful, and a chance at a sacfest once I've tucked my cat away in a
room.  Is it worth using the charging scroll on the BoT at this stage?
It will help me level up, as well as perhaps getting me some nice
things.  I'd like to get some holy water as well.  Once Mandy has
cleared out the guards (no problem for her) I can dip for water with
one of my un-id'd potions.  I think it might be a good idea to level
up a bit before dipping.

The only box I've found so far is an ice box.  Can this be used as a
stash box?  I'm worried about freezing my potions.

I'm going to try and put all the lessons I've learnt with my healers
to good use in future, so I hope to take this one further than I've
been before, at least.  I am a very poor player, though.

